Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed Package
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Added Analytics Component
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/next'
- Added the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element (before closing `</body>` tag)
- Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

## Implementation Details:

The Analytics component was added following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified the project uses Next.js 16.1.6 with App Router (based on src/app directory structure)
- Added Analytics component to the root layout.tsx file
- Placed component at the end of the body element, after all providers and content
- Used the framework-specific import from '@vercel/analytics/next'

## Files Modified:

1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
3. `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Verification:

- TypeScript type checking passed with no errors related to the Analytics component
- Code structure preserved with proper indentation and formatting
- Existing providers and components remain unchanged
- Analytics component added at the correct location per official documentation

## Next Steps:

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Verify successful setup by checking for network requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` endpoints
3. Monitor analytics data in the Vercel dashboard Analytics section

The implementation follows best practices and integrates seamlessly with the existing application structure.
